{"kind":"finding","id":"F-catchall-025-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/EndOfRecordingWalkbackTests.cs","line":526,"method":"WalkbackSubdivided_ZeroStepMeters_ClampsToDefault","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/SpawnCollisionDetector.cs:577; clamp to 0.1f instead of DefaultWalkbackStepMeters -> test stays green","what_it_asserts":"A zero stepMeters still returns found for a one-point trajectory and logs a warn containing 'invalid stepMeters'.","why_weak":"The clamp VALUE is never observed: one point clears on the base case before any sub-stepping, and the log assertion stops before the 'clamping to N' half of the line.","proposed_action":"Use a two-point segment with an all-overlap predicate and assert the sub-step call count equals ceil(d / DefaultWalkbackStepMeters) + 1, or extend the log assertion to the clamping-to token.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-catchall-025-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/EndOfRecordingWalkbackTests.cs","line":374,"method":"WalkbackSubdivided_InterpolatesLatLonLinearly","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"medium","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/SpawnCollisionDetector.cs:571+; swap the sub-step lerp endpoints -> this and WalkbackSubdivided_LastPointOverlaps_FindsFirstClearSubStep both red","what_it_asserts":"With the clear on call 4 (k=3), result.lat equals lerp(segEnd, segStart, 3/n).","why_weak":"Identical act and assertion to the cell at line 281; the only differences are segment length (6 m vs 10 m) and assertion precision (10 vs 8 digits). Neither reaches a branch the other misses.","proposed_action":"Merge the two into one Theory over segment length, keeping the tighter precision.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
